msgid "Add the `quarkus-data-hibernate` and `quarkus-jdbc-postgresql` extensions:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The first extension, `quarkus-data-hibernate`, provides everything you need for database access.\n"
"The second, `quarkus-jdbc-postgresql`, is the JDBC driver that lets Quarkus connect to a PostgreSQL database.\n"
"If you use a different database, such as MySQL, MariaDB, or H2, pick the corresponding `quarkus-jdbc-*` driver instead (see xref:datasource.adoc#configure-a-jdbc-datasource[Configure a JDBC datasource]).\n"
"Quarkus Data Hibernate cannot work without a JDBC driver <<reactive,or a reactive SQL client>>."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Quarkus Data Hibernate (Panache Next) and the classic Panache (Panache 1) extensions cannot be used together.\n"
"Adding both `quarkus-data-hibernate` and any classic Panache extension\n"
"(such as `quarkus-hibernate-orm-panache`, `quarkus-hibernate-orm-panache-kotlin`,\n"
"`quarkus-hibernate-reactive-panache` or `quarkus-hibernate-reactive-panache-kotlin`) to the same\n"
"application makes the build fail with an explicit error.\n"
"These two data access layers are mutually\n"
"exclusive, so pick only one of them."
msgstr ""

msgid "Add the annotation processor configuration to your build file."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Quarkus Data Hibernate uses the Quarkus Data annotation processor, a key component that reads your repository interfaces at compile time, validates queries, and generates implementation classes.\n"
"These generated classes are compiled together with your code and wired up automatically by Quarkus.\n"
"They are also simple to read if you want to understand how they work internally."
msgstr ""

